  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 8th level, the bumbler gains the improved uncanny dodge class feature of the rogue (as described in Chapter 3 of the Pathfinder Core Rulebook). They can no longer be flanked. This defense denies a rogue the ability to sneak attack the bumbler by flanking them, unless the attacker has at least four more rogue levels than the bumbler has bumbler class levels.</p>\n<p>If a bumbler already has uncanny dodge (see above) from another class, the levels from the classes that grant uncanny dodge stack to determine the minimum rogue level required to flank the bumbler.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/bumbler#toc18\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
